Hi,

a while ago we startet the vis server project. Its aim is to supply a topology 
layout of the batman network. To overcome the problem that every node just 
knows its very own horizon we designed a vis server which collects vis 
topology messages from every node and generates the well known dot draw 
output. This output can be used by various programs to render a topology 
graphic. I just made some screenshots of our network rendered by olsrs3d (see 
s3d.berlios.de). 
You can find them here: https://www.open-mesh.net/batman/vis
I will update the pictures once more hosts in Berlin have activated that 
feature and thus are visible on our topology.

Regards,
Marek

